   "caption": "Each line is one ISS run; each point is the median over all accepted frames in a ~1 mm bin. The spacing keeps evolving along most runs (INIT-4 +22%, S2-4 +49%, S1-4 -13%, S2-11 +47% from onset to end), so the \"steady\" value is a late-run value, not a converged one. HD-9 is planar (no points) until ~28 mm. No Earth control is included: this shows pattern dynamics in microgravity, not a microgravity advantage."
  },
